// check: refuse E_InitPerformsOwnOp
// An install's config argument runs before the install exists, so a perform
// there of an op only this handler answers reaches nothing. The judgment
// refuses at the install, as it refuses the same perform in a state init or
// a config default. On boot 7c3be609 only the emit's walk found it, so
// `mentl check` judged this program clean and exited 0.
effect F {
  g() -> Int
}

handler hf(k: Int) {
  g() => resume(k),
}

fn main() = (g()) ~> hf(g())
